## 5. Failure Modes & Chaos Engineering

In a highly distributed, stateful system running non-deterministic AI agent workflows, failure is a certainty. We design for resiliency by anticipating split-brain scenarios, cascading downstream rate-limits, and resource exhaustion.

### Split-Brain Mitigation via Fencing Tokens

If a network partition occurs, the control plane might assume an Orchestration Node has failed and attempt to rehydrate its active actors on a healthy node. This can result in two instances of the same `Agent ID` running concurrently (a violation of Invariant 1).

To mitigate this, we implement **Epoch-based Fencing Tokens**. Every state write to the distributed state store must include the actor's active epoch number, which is incremented by the control plane upon actor rehydration. 

```
